course: dictionary
lesson: 8482
title: A word with many homes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sanctuary is a safe place where someone or something is protected from harm. Most often it is a place for animals or people who need protecting. «Some people want zoos turned into sanctuaries that only rescue animals.» Here, sanctuaries are places that rescue animals and keep them safe.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «They found sanctuary in the church» tells you that sanctuary is the safety people find when they are in danger. Swap in your meaning: «They found safety in the church» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Sanctuary can also mean a calm, private place where you feel peaceful. «My bedroom is my sanctuary» does not mean a place to hide from danger. It means a place where you can relax and feel at peace. Read the whole sentence to know which meaning the writer chose.
fact: A sanctuary is a safe place where someone or something is protected.
fact: A wildlife sanctuary protects animals, and «donkey sanctuary» and «bird sanctuary» are examples of places that care for animals.
fact: In the Middle Ages, people in danger could claim sanctuary in a church.
fact: In a church, the sanctuary is the holiest part, near the altar.
fact: Useful phrases: seek sanctuary, find sanctuary, give sanctuary.
exercise: «Healesville Sanctuary near Melbourne keeps only Australian animals.» What is a sanctuary here? | A cold place full of ice | A shop that sells animals | A school for zoo keepers | *A safe place where animals are protected
exercise: «They found sanctuary in the church.» What does sanctuary mean? | *Safety from danger | A long journey | A loud noise | Dinner
exercise: «My bedroom is my sanctuary.» What does sanctuary suggest? | A place full of noisy visitors | A pet shop | A busy road | *A calm, private place where you feel peaceful
test: Which phrase means to offer protection to someone in danger? | Give a present | *Give sanctuary | Give up | Give way
test: «The belugas were moved to a sea sanctuary.» What kind of place is a sea sanctuary? | A school for sailors | A busy harbour for ships | A shop selling fish | *A safe place where animals are protected
exam: Which sentence uses sanctuary to mean the holy part of a church? | The belugas were moved to a sea sanctuary | My bedroom is my sanctuary | Donkeys crowded in a shed to stay dry | *The altar stands at the front of the sanctuary of the church
